lines[11]:
  - i, text, start, end
  - 0, What happens if you swallow your gum?, 0.4, 2.222
  - 1, "Well, it slides down your throat and lands right in your stomach,", 2.502, 5.762
  - 2, where strong acid gets to work on it., 6.312, 8.465
  - 3, "The sugar and flavor dissolve pretty quickly, but the gum base is a different story.", 8.745, 13.831
  - 4, "It's a rubbery polymer, and your body simply can't break it down.", 14.111, 17.96
  - 5, "So does it stay there for seven years? Nope, that's a total myth.", 18.24, 22.078
  - 6, "Your gut just keeps pushing it along,", 22.358, 24.268
  - 7, "and within a few days, it's out of your system.", 24.798, 27.096
  - 8, "But if you swallow a lot of gum all at once,", 27.376, 29.846
  - 9, it can clump together and actually block your gut., 30.246, 32.938
  - 10, "So maybe, just spit it out.", 33.218, 34.774
